# Linux
```bash
mkdir -p supply_chain_monitor/docs/architecture
```
###the -p flag stands for "parents".###

It safely ensures the whole directory structure exists in one go.

So essentially, -p = "create the full path if needed, and don’t complain if it’s already there."

---


```bash
python3 -c "import pandas; import sklearn; import fastapi; print('Everything is working!')"
```
### the -c flag means "execute the following command string".
The command after -c is treated as Python code.

It's commonly used in: Shell scripts, Dockerfiles, CI/CD pipelines, Quick checks to see if a package is installed


# Setting up a virtual environement

```
# Create the isolated environment container
python3 -m venv venv

# Activate the virtual environment
source venv/bin/activate

# Upgrade pip to secure reliable wheels compilation
pip install --upgrade pip

# Install the pinned project manifest
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Build/upgrade the requirements.txt
pip freeze > requirements.txt
```

